IcedTea integration
-------------------

This directory contains patches needed for building IcedTea 3.x with
this version of JamVM.  The patches are formatted for IcedTea's patch
mechanism, which applies them with patch -p0 from the IcedTea build
directory; to apply them to a plain JamVM tree instead, use patch -p2.


Building IcedTea 3.x with JamVM 2.1.0
-------------------------------------

Verified with IcedTea 3.40.1 on GNU/Linux aarch64 and x86_64.
Check IcedTea's own INSTALL file for its build requirements.

1. Download and unpack the IcedTea sources:

     https://icedtea.classpath.org/download/source/icedtea-3.40.1.tar.xz

2. Update IcedTea's JamVM patches.  IcedTea carries patches for an
   old pre-2.0.0 JamVM snapshot; all of them are already merged in
   JamVM 2.1.0.  JamVM 2.1.0 instead needs unsafe-natives.patch from
   this directory:

     cp <jamvm>/contrib/icedtea/unsafe-natives.patch patches/jamvm/

   In Makefile.am, replace the four patches/jamvm/ lines in the
   ICEDTEA_PATCHES block with the new one:

     if BUILD_JAMVM
     ICEDTEA_PATCHES += patches/jamvm/unsafe-natives.patch
     endif

   Then regenerate the build system:

     ./autogen.sh

3. Configure and build.  Pass the path of the JamVM release tarball
   to configure, along with its SHA-256 checksum.  Note that JFR
   support must be disabled (--disable-jfr), since it depends on
   HotSpot metadata that JamVM does not provide.

     mkdir build && cd build
     ../configure \
       --enable-jamvm \
       --with-jamvm-src-zip=<path>/jamvm-2.1.0.tar.gz \
       --with-jamvm-checksum=<published sha256> \
       --with-jdk-home=<path to a JDK 8> \
       --disable-bootstrap \
       --disable-jfr \
       --disable-docs
     make

   IcedTea downloads the OpenJDK source drops itself and verifies
   their checksums.

4. The built image is in openjdk.build/images/j2sdk-image:

     $ openjdk.build/images/j2sdk-image/bin/java -version
     openjdk version "1.8.0_512"
     IcedTea Runtime Environment (3.40.1) (linux-gnu build 1.8.0_512-b01)
     JamVM (build 2.1.0, inline-threaded interpreter with stack-caching)
